  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>autoML - blends the retailer's four files into one training set, writes H2O.csv, and ranks models with H2O
AutoML.
Needs the h2o-env virtual environment (Prerequisite Tasks); the four CSV files sit beside it.

1. csvi-customer: Text file input, customer.csv, the first 10,000 customers.
2. csvi_customer_billing, csvi-customer transaction, csvi-transaction_fraud_report: CSV file input, the billing,
   order and fraud report files.
3. slkp-customer, slkp-transaction_details, slkp-transaction_fraud_report: Stream lookup, one row per
   transaction.
4. frmla-billing_shipping_zip_equal: Formula, billing_shipping_zip_equal = [customer_billing_zip] =
   [ship_to_zip].
5. sv-change_to_numbers: Select values, the nine fields, the four flags as Number 1 and 0.
6. tfo-H2O: Text file output, data/H2O.csv, semicolons, no header.
7. auto machine learning: Python Executor, h2o-env's python.exe, All rows as dataset; H2O AutoML, up to
   five models ranked by AUC; the best saved in automl_output.

Shipped data: 9,999 rows in data/H2O.csv; one row back with best_algorithm gbm, best_auc 0.9951 and
models_trained 5.</note>
